# Code Style

## Purpose

Apply when editing Go, Lua, or sqlc SQL. Layout follows `structure.mdc`. Naming follows `naming.mdc`. Cold-path detail: `cold-path.mdc`. Slop gates: `anti-slop.mdc`.

## Package layout

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Domain packages | One package per functional domain under `internal/<name>/` |
| Allowed subdirs | `db/`, `queries/`, `migrations/`, `pb/` (generated), domain sub-slices (e.g. `internal/fraud/admin/`) |
| Banned ceremony | `dto/`, `usecase/`, `providers/`, `repositories/` subtrees |
| `cmd/` | `main.go` wires config and modules only; no business logic in `main` |
| `pkg/` | No `internal/` imports |
| `doc.go` | **Mandatory** at package root — `package <name>` only (`naming.mdc`, `modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| `internal/domain` | Shared hot-path vocabulary only (no json/db tags) |

## File naming

| Pattern | Example |
| :--- | :--- |
| Production | snake_case `<role>_<rest>.go` — `track_core.go`, `runtime_patch.go` |
| Package-local | Inside `internal/<domain>/`, omit the package name from the filename (`dto.go`, not `campaign_dto.go` in `internal/campaign/`) — `naming.mdc` |
| Composition root | Cross-domain files in `controlplane` keep domain token: `campaign_runtime_bridge.go` |
| Bridge in controlplane | `fraudadmin_bridge.go` — domain token OK outside domain package |
| Split threshold | Near 500 lines or when transport mixes with core logic |
| **Banned new** | `*_aliases.go`, `service_<domain>_*.go` in controlplane, `<domain>_<role>.go` inside `internal/<domain>/` |
| God package | >40 prod `.go` files or ~8k LOC — split (`modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| Micro-package | New domain dir without handlers/store + wire in same PR — forbidden (`modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| Bridge file | <=200 lines; wiring only — no domain rules (`modular-monolith.mdc`) |
| Tests | `*_test.go`, `*_bench_test.go`, `*_fault_test.go` beside code |

## Types and tags

| Layer | Convention |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hot path | `internal/campaignmodel` / hot `internal/domain` - no struct tags |
| sqlc rows | `internal/<svc>/db` - `db.Campaign` |
| Admin JSON | `FooDTO` with `json:"snake_case"` in handler/service files |
| Replica/pubsub | `fooReplicaDTO` with json tags near serialization |
| I/O boundary | Map in one step: `db.Row -> toFooDTO()` or `db.Row -> campaignmodel.Campaign` |

Banned: parallel Entity/Model/View for the same table.

## Errors

| Path | Convention |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hot (`internal/ingestion`, `internal/rtb`) | Typed rejects (`NoBidReason`, `filterRejectKind`), pre-built response bytes; no `fmt.Errorf` on `/track`; no dynamic Prometheus labels |
| Cold | Sentinels in `errors.go`, `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`, `errors.Is` at HTTP boundary via `mapServiceError` / `writeServiceError` |
| Precedence | Hot path wins over idiomatic Go where they conflict (`core.mdc` SLA) |

## Codegen

```bash
make gen # sqlc -> internal/*/db/
make proto # buf -> internal/*/pb/
```

After proto sync run `go run ./cmd/patch-vtproto-hotpath` for hot ingest paths.

Do not hand-edit generated `*.pb.go`, `*.sql.go`, bpf2go outputs.

## PR verification

| Surface | Command |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hot path | `make test-alloc-gate`; benchmem 0 allocs on touched hot benchmarks |
| Cold path | `go test ./... -short` for touched packages |
| Lint | `make lint` before merge |
| Perf-sensitive | `scripts/test/gate_run.sh` or CI `perf-gate.yaml` |

## Banned patterns

- Repository interfaces over sqlc, Provider/Factory maps, `map[string]any` JSON builders.
- HTMX admin fragments - JSON `/api/v1` only (`control-plane.mdc`).

